    },
    "message": "Let one program take a person out and bring them back\n\nThe plan check refused a return whose person was still present at the\nfork, even when the same program took them out earlier. It now accepts\nthat pairing. If the exit is deferred while the person is busy (#181) past\nthe program's return, the exit is dropped and the return skipped, both\nrecorded as suppressed, as an exit deferred past its expected return\nalready is. No coefficient changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
